  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"113\" data-end=\"313\">The <strong data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"139\">blood cadmium test</strong> measures the concentration of cadmium in the bloodstream&mdash;a <strong data-start=\"199\" data-end=\"220\">toxic heavy metal</strong> found in industrial environments, tobacco smoke, contaminated food, and certain fertilizers.</p>\n<p data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"336\">This test is used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"338\" data-end=\"680\">\n<li data-start=\"338\" data-end=\"426\">\n<p data-start=\"340\" data-end=\"426\">Detect <strong data-start=\"347\" data-end=\"373\">acute cadmium exposure</strong> (typically from inhalation in occupational settings)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"427\" data-end=\"529\">\n<p data-start=\"429\" data-end=\"529\">Monitor <strong data-start=\"437\" data-end=\"457\">chronic exposure</strong> in individuals at risk (e.g., battery manufacturing, welding, smelting)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"530\" data-end=\"635\">\n<p data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"635\">Evaluate potential <strong data-start=\"551\" data-end=\"572\">toxicity symptoms</strong> (e.g., kidney damage, bone demineralization, lung dysfunction)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"636\" data-end=\"680\">\n<p data-start=\"638\" data-end=\"680\">Support diagnosis of <strong data-start=\"659\" data-end=\"680\">cadmium poisoning</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong data-start=\"659\" data-end=\"680\">Elevated Blood Cadmium &ndash; Clinical Implications</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition / Scenario</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Occupational or environmental exposure</strong></td>\n<td>High levels may indicate <strong>recent or acute exposure</strong>, especially via inhalation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Chronic cadmium toxicity</strong></td>\n<td>May result in <strong>renal tubular damage</strong>, proteinuria, and decreased GFR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Lung damage</strong></td>\n<td>Inhalation of cadmium fumes can cause <strong>pulmonary edema or emphysema</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bone effects</strong></td>\n<td>Long-term exposure may lead to <strong>osteomalacia or osteoporosis</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cardiovascular/metabolic effects</strong></td>\n<td>Associated with <strong>hypertension, diabetes risk, and atherosclerosis</strong> in chronic cases</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
